WEBVTT

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:06.310
<i>Once upon a time,</i>

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:10.510
<i>there was an alien, a cyborg,</i>

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:14.240
<i>an ammonite, the Kumamoto 
Castle, a Shiba dog,</i>

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.570
<i>a sea monkey, and a bok choy,</i>

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.460
<i>and they all lived together.</i>

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:55.460
<b>Doggy & Scramble</b>

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:20.990
Natsume-san.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.110
Murakami-senpai.

00:02:23.110 --> 00:02:25.500
What are you writing today?

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.250
I'm working on the novel I've been writing.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:32.120
Oh, you said it's due soon, right?

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.750
For the lit club's mini-magazine.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:37.060
No, I finished that already.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:40.560
This is a novel I've been 
writing for a long time.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.120
For a long time?

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:42.940
Yes.

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:44.680
Since elementary school.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.100
That long ago?

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:48.840
What type of story is it?

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.700
Well, simply put, an alien, a cyborg,

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:53.720
an ammonite, the Kumamoto 
Castle, a Shiba dog,

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:58.020
a sea monkey, and a bok choy all 
work together to save the world.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:02:59.530
Huh?

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:01.740
Bok choy?

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.490
It falls into the space opera genre.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:09.740
It's an action adventure story that makes 
the blood race and the flesh dance.

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:10.840
Right.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:13.320
But I have writer's block.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.880
I have up until the climax written,

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.880
but I'm not sure how to end it.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:19.720
I see.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:25.050
I work on it now and then, but I haven't gotten far.

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.790
And you've been working on 
it since elementary school?

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:28.760
That's right.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:31.420
I've rewritten it plenty of times,

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:34.490
so the story keeps changing, but...

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:35.750
I see.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.690
I know, Natsume-san.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:41.920
If you wouldn't mind, may I read your story?

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:43.590
Read this?

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:44.520
Yes.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:48.910
Maybe I could help you come up 
with ideas for how to continue it.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:50.710
That's true.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:53.330
Would you take a look at it, then?

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:02.720
<i>Once upon a time,</i>

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.970
<i>there was an alien, a cyborg,</i>

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:08.960
<i>an ammonite, the Kumamoto 
Castle, a Shiba dog,</i>

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.850
<i>a sea monkey, and a bok choy, 
and they all lived together.</i>

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:13.990
Why?

00:04:13.990 --> 00:04:15.500
Why did this have to happen?!

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.980
If something isn't done, Earth will be destroyed!

00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:23.280
Why did you keep quiet about that until now?!

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.820
What should we do, Kumamoto Castle?

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.860
Asking me won't do any good.

00:04:27.860 --> 00:04:32.250
I know. Maybe Bok Choy knows something.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:37.350
Uh, so the Kumamoto Castle 
can speak Japanese?

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:39.460
Yes, since he is a Japanese castle.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.950
But the alien can't?

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:45.210
The alien speaks in alien language.

00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:47.310
Also, when he came to Earth,

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:50.360
he began learning the 
standard language, Esperanto.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.080
I see.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.930
Also, the bok choy is a really pretty girl.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.960
What is this, ruff?!

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:59.080
Why is everyone just sitting here, ruff?!

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:01.280
If we don't hurry, Bok Choy will be in danger!

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.900
Quiet down a bit.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.610
You keep screaming like that,

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:08.240
and people will think your 
owner didn't train you, Baby.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:09.610
What was that?!

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:12.040
Try saying that again, ruff!

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:16.090
Who's this monkey wearing the goggles?

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:17.560
That's the sea monkey.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:20.460
Aren't sea monkeys a type of plankton?

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:22.660
When I started writing this,

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:26.890
I thought that sea monkeys were 
monkeys that lived in the sea.

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:27.840
Oh...

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:45.110
This is good.

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:47.910
Natsume-san, this is really good!

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.860
Oh, uh, thanks.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:52.920
You should be more proud.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.040
This really is good.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:57.040
Um...

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:00.180
I've rewritten it so many times,

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:04.420
I'm not quite sure if it's even 
good to other people anymore.

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:08.160
It's good. I guarantee it.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:10.600
Reading it was very exciting.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:14.180
So what happens to Bok Choy after that?

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:19.670
I was thinking of having her 
die protecting the alien.

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:20.900
She's going to die?!

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.730
Hmm... Maybe not.

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:25.860
Wh-Which is it?

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:32.590
I... haven't decided yet, I guess?

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:33.740
I see.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:37.030
I really want to know what happens.

00:06:37.030 --> 00:06:39.730
When are you going to finish this?

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:42.130
At my current pace,

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:45.170
I might never finish.

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:46.600
What?!

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:50.600
Well, whatever happens, happens.

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:53.300
Writing is an adventure in exploration.

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:58.960
Ryunosuke Akutagawa said that 
after you've done whatever you can,

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:01.880
you can only rely on heaven for the rest.

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.310
I see.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.420
Fumio-san?

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:13.170
Why do you look so glum?

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:15.330
Oh, Chloe-san.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:18.410
Did something badly happen?

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:21.450
"Something bad," you mean?

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:24.280
I was wondering how it ended.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:25.740
Ended?

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:28.420
Natsume-san is writing a novel,

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:30.350
and it was really interesting,

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:31.680
so I wanted to know how it ended.

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:35.680
Oh! I love novels, too!

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.060
I want to read it, too!

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:39.960
Want to read it?

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.310
I borrowed it.

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:54.320
What happens to Bok Choy?!

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.200
Apparently, she might die.

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:01.240
She also might not die.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:03.330
Which one?

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:06.630
Natsume-san doesn't know yet, either.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:10.040
I want to know.

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:13.200
Me, too.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:15.170
Let me borrow this.

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:15.720
Huh?

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:18.030
This is so good.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:20.430
It's wasted if everyone else doesn't read it!

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.760
Hey, wait!

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.210
That was so touching!

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:31.440
What happens?! I want to know!

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:37.280
What is this?

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:39.120
It's really good!

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:47.130
What happens to Bok Choy?!

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:50.590
Huh?

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.740
We want to read the rest.

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:00.780
I can't stop thinking about how it ends.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:03.960
I can turn it into a manga for you!

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:06.480
What about Bok Choy? What about Bok Choy?!

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:09.070
That's what happened.

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:09.820
Right.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:15.500
We came here to get you 
worked down to write the rest.

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:17.200
You mean "worked up."

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:19.600
Yeah, but...

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:23.750
I've been working on this for 
years, and it's still not done.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:25.960
I don't know if I can just finish it like that.

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:27.800
I see.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:30.680
I know why you can't finish it.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:31.470
Hm?

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:36.720
You're missing something essential as a writer.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.600
Something essential?

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:40.100
What's that?

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:44.850
Something you must have to finish a work.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:45.850
That is...

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.390
<b>Deadline</b>

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.390
A deadline!

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:54.650
If I don't have a deadline, I just keep 
goofing off and never finish my manga.

00:09:55.160 --> 00:09:58.200
But if I don't, it won't be ready in time for the expo.

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.860
When it gets to that point, I feel motivated,

00:10:00.860 --> 00:10:02.410
and I finish it off.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:03.880
I see.

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:05.580
That makes sense.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:08.150
I always finish my cosplay outfits early

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:11.520
before it's time to fit them.

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:14.500
I guess it's like summer homework.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:16.770
That's why you just need to set a deadline

00:10:16.770 --> 00:10:19.590
and finish before then.

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:22.010
That's a great idea.

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:25.410
So, when do we set the deadline?

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:28.050
I want to read the ending now.

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:30.100
How about tomorrow?

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:31.610
Not possible.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:33.270
What about next week, then?

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:36.740
It might take longer than that.

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:38.650
The week after next?

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:40.570
I'm not sure...

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:42.760
What about the week after that?

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:44.440
That'd be hard...

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:46.050
Then, next month?

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:48.080
We have finals, so...

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.060
What about next year?

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:51.750
I'm not sure about that...

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:55.130
I can't wait that long!

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:58.650
If it's hard to finish it all at once,

00:10:58.650 --> 00:11:02.520
then why not try setting smaller 
deadlines, and go from there?

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:04.470
Like a weekly publication?

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:07.640
It might be easier to do small bits weekly.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.950
Natsume-san, how does that sound?

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:13.440
Yeah, I'll do my best.

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:14.560
Really?!

00:11:14.920 --> 00:11:18.490
Yes, I want to finish it, too.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:21.570
Well then, the sooner, the better.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:24.470
We're looking forward to it.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:29.070
Girl Friend BETA.

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:50.100
Um,

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:54.420
are you guys waiting for me to finish writing?

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:59.070
Murakami-senpai...

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:06.450
Hm? Where's Natsume-san?

00:12:07.000 --> 00:12:09.370
Oh, she isn't here yet?

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:12.550
The novel's supposed to be due today.

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:15.530
I thought I'd be able to read the rest...

00:12:16.480 --> 00:12:18.480
This isn't good.

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:19.960
Did she run away?

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:20.840
What?

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:24.560
Authors who can't make their deadlines

00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:26.760
run away from their editors all the time.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:27.760
What?

00:12:28.120 --> 00:12:29.870
That's terrible.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:31.670
What should we do?

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:34.640
The thing an editor should 
do when this happens...

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:37.650
is find her, of course!

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.890
That sounds like a lot of trouble.

00:12:41.890 --> 00:12:46.960
I would have finished it a long 
time ago if it were that simple.

00:12:47.930 --> 00:12:49.030
Yeah.

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:52.290
Is it that hard to write, though?

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.280
You finish your stuff for the school newspaper

00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:58.670
and your romance novels really fast.

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:01.840
Yeah, because one's more a hobby of mine,

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.960
and the newspaper has a deadline.

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:07.040
But aren't you writing that as a hobby,

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:09.210
and don't you have a deadline now, too?

00:13:10.640 --> 00:13:12.640
Let me read it.

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:13.640
No.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:15.050
Why?

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:18.570
I don't want you telling me you 
want to read the rest of it, too.

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:20.280
It's that good, then?

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:22.690
Not so much good...

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:27.200
I just like writing it.

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.120
Huh...

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:30.200
Oh!

00:13:30.520 --> 00:13:32.950
I found you, Natsume-san.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:36.120
It's time to write the ending!

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:46.670
Natsume-san, you haven't written the 
ending to the novel yet, have you?

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:49.590
I just don't have any idea what to do.

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:51.930
Indeed...

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:54.170
We have no other choice.

00:13:54.170 --> 00:13:58.310
We'll just have to help you get ideas, then.

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:00.150
Help?

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:03.370
We need to find people to help.

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:05.720
We'll get ideas that way.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:08.090
Can we even do that?

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:10.660
It's important not to rush.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:11.280
Huh?

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:18.070
The Heroes Who Seem Strong 
But Aren't, Except Maybe a Little

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:14.940
We need to go around asking people

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:18.080
who know about the characters in this story.

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:19.830
I get it.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:23.130
We all belong to a lot of different clubs.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:26.450
I bet there are people who are 
knowledgeable about this stuff.

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:30.010
So we ask those people, and get ideas.

00:14:30.610 --> 00:14:33.600
The characters are...

00:14:33.910 --> 00:14:36.850
Let's split up and ask people!

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:39.060
Right!

00:14:39.720 --> 00:14:41.930
Aliens?

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:44.360
I know a lot about science fiction movies.

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:46.770
That's great!

00:14:46.770 --> 00:14:49.200
So, about the alien in this story...

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:52.100
According to the description,

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:54.330
this seems like a large-nosed grey.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.910
Not a reptilian, right?

00:14:56.910 --> 00:14:59.710
Doesn't seem like a Nordic, either.

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:03.610
I am an android, yes,

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:05.710
but I am not a cyborg.

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:09.440
Are androids and cyborgs different?

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:11.450
Yes, they are.

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:14.850
They're as different as crab 
pilaf and imitation crab.

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:16.250
That's great.

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:18.250
You're basically the same, then.

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:19.970
Look at this.

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:20.600
Huh?

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:23.680
I know a lot about ammonites.

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:25.860
Also, I know about trilobites
 and nautiluses, too.

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.190
Really? That's great.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.880
What about sea monkeys?

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:31.490
I know about them.

00:15:31.920 --> 00:15:36.380
The brine shrimp, like Artemia, 
that you keep in aquariums, right?

00:15:36.380 --> 00:15:38.560
They're creatures in the Chirocephalidae family,

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:40.720
Anostraca order, subclass Sarsostraca, right?

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.520
Not those sea monkeys.

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:46.080
This is a monkey that lives in the sea.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:47.000
Huh?

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:54.010
Thanks for getting all of this together, but...

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:57.010
I feel like there's more people now.

00:15:57.330 --> 00:16:00.700
I want to know what happens 
so badly, I can't study.

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:03.600
I'm psyched now. You've gotta do something!

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:05.900
Please write the ending.

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:08.270
You let them read it, didn't you?

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:12.570
Well, we needed to so we could get their help.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:14.660
Yeah, so please!

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:16.830
Et tu, Tsugumi?

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:18.900
But this is pretty impressive.

00:16:18.900 --> 00:16:19.630
Huh?

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:23.080
There are so many people here 
who want to read your story.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:27.830
I thought it was a weird novel at first,

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:29.000
but as I was reading it,

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:30.640
it was so interesting,

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:33.220
I just got engrossed in it.

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:37.720
It's incredible that you were able to 
write a novel this good, Natsume-san.

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:42.930
Natsume-san?

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:45.470
If my readers think so highly of me,

00:16:45.470 --> 00:16:47.940
I guess I'm going to have to write it.

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:49.480
Then...

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.820
Can I use this research you got for me?

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.570
Sure!

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:41.580
Natsume-san.

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:45.240
It's almost time to close the library.

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:47.420
Is it that late?

00:17:48.220 --> 00:17:50.790
Can I stay just a little bit longer?

00:17:50.790 --> 00:17:53.170
I want to finish this one part.

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:55.800
That's fine.

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:57.680
Thank you.

00:17:58.480 --> 00:18:01.670
But are you sure you should push yourself so hard?

00:18:01.670 --> 00:18:06.430
I have tons of fun when I work on this novel.

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:09.540
I forget what time it is and just get absorbed.

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:10.860
I see.

00:18:11.250 --> 00:18:14.220
So it isn't stressful at all.

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:15.980
It's a lot of work,

00:18:15.980 --> 00:18:17.740
but it isn't painful for me.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:23.400
When I write, I get stuck, tripped up,

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:24.920
and I backtrack a lot,

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:30.000
but when the alien and Bok 
Choy cry and laugh together,

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.790
I feel like I want to know how it ends, too.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:37.710
That's why I have a lot of fun doing this.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:39.860
But...

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:45.060
But I wonder why I couldn't write it until now...

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:54.940
<i>Before they realized it,</i>

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:59.850
<i>they all found themselves 
working towards one goal.</i>

00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:01.860
<i>They all wanted one thing:</i>

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:04.830
<i>they wanted to protect this small,</i>

00:19:05.260 --> 00:19:07.330
<i>but precious world.</i>

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:11.830
<i>And they all felt strongly about it.</i>

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:13.850
This is wonderful!

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:15.280
It's a masterpiece.

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:18.360
I've never read a novel this fun before!

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:19.800
She got me!

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:21.840
I didn't expect this ending.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:23.470
I'm so happy...

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:26.160
I'm so happy for Bok Choy.

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.390
That was a great novel, Natsume-san.

00:19:28.760 --> 00:19:31.180
I'd love to reread this over and over.

00:19:31.180 --> 00:19:33.400
I wouldn't go that far...

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:37.740
I started crying when I thought 
the alien was going to die.

00:19:37.740 --> 00:19:40.190
I cried there, too.

00:19:40.190 --> 00:19:44.280
I felt bad that the cyborg 
was going to be left all alone.

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:48.920
And then it's really cool how the 
ammonite kicks butt after that.

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:50.080
Yeah.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:52.420
Who would have thought the ammonite 
would come to save the day?

00:19:56.240 --> 00:20:01.220
Isn't it great that everyone loved it so much?

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:02.800
Y-Yeah...

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:04.170
I guess so.

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:11.920
Natsume-san?

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:14.650
It's over...

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:16.120
Huh?

00:20:16.760 --> 00:20:19.650
The novel's done...

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:22.030
Natsume-san...

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:28.340
I realized why I couldn't write the ending until now.

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:33.160
I didn't want to leave this story.

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:37.070
I love this story.

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:39.200
I love Bok Choy and the others.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:43.740
I wanted to continue playing 
around in their world.

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:48.220
I didn't want to let it end.

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:50.280
Natsume-san...

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:54.230
That's why I couldn't finish it.

00:20:57.480 --> 00:21:00.460
But I'm sure this was for the best.

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:01.230
Huh?

00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:04.870
If I didn't finish it,

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:07.170
and left everyone hanging,

00:21:07.170 --> 00:21:09.700
I'd feel bad for Bok Choy and the rest.

00:21:10.430 --> 00:21:12.760
Thank you, everyone.

00:21:12.760 --> 00:21:15.950
Thank you for helping me 
write this wonderful ending.

00:21:15.950 --> 00:21:18.960
I'm sure Bok Choy and the rest are happy, too.

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:33.340
The Heroes Who Seem Strong 
But Aren't, Except Maybe a Little

00:21:42.750 --> 00:21:43.960
Chloe-san...

00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:46.200
Fumio-san...

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:48.960
Everyone, are you...

00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:52.600
Well, you know...

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:55.500
Everyone...

00:21:59.450 --> 00:22:02.090
You guys were late today.

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:04.340
Natsume-san?

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:05.830
The Heroes Who Seem Strong 
But Aren't, Except They Got Stronger

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:08.420
Here. Could you read this?

00:22:08.420 --> 00:22:09.760
What is it?

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:12.510
"Once upon a time,

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:15.530
there was an alien, a cyborg,

00:22:15.530 --> 00:22:18.600
an ammonite, the Kumamoto 
Castle, a Shiba dog,

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:21.940
a sea monkey, and bok choy, 
and they all lived together.

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:26.130
After a fierce battle, they protected the Earth,

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:28.720
and peace returned to the world,

00:22:28.720 --> 00:22:34.160
but that was only the start of a larger battle."

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:36.200
Natsume-san, is this...

00:22:36.510 --> 00:22:39.500
Is it the continuation to the novel?

00:22:39.820 --> 00:22:42.750
I guess the story wasn't over.

00:22:44.080 --> 00:22:47.260
Bok Choy and the others said 
they aren't done having fun,

00:22:47.780 --> 00:22:51.260
so I decided to have fun with them a little longer.

00:22:52.880 --> 00:22:54.230
Natsume-san!

00:22:54.640 --> 00:22:58.290
Everyone, that was only the prologue.

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:01.840
They're about to have an even 
greater adventure together.

00:23:03.220 --> 00:23:07.400
So please help me come 
up with ideas for the rest.

00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:09.400
What?

00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:24.890
<b>Preview</b>

00:24:11.340 --> 00:24:12.720
Welcome!

00:24:12.720 --> 00:24:14.140
Oh, Kokomi-chan.

00:24:14.140 --> 00:24:18.060
Sasahara-senpai, I'd like a refreshing drink, please.

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:21.430
I have something cute and tasty that'll be perfect.

00:24:20.980 --> 00:24:24.890
<b>Episode 8: On the Other Side of the Cream Soda</b>

00:24:21.430 --> 00:24:24.560
Next time: On the Other Side of the Cream Soda.
